aking: introduces new elements AND changes relationship between lab's R&D and its compliance obligations, or addresses larger problem of what lab researches\n3 = paradigm stretching: changes that relationship (e.g., logging woven into science, new partners...)\n2 = slightly paradigm stretching: introduces new elements (tools, formats, processes) but still treats compliance as logging practice\n1 = paradigm preserving: standard compliance and logging practice; lab's way unchanged\n\nWrapper isolates restrictive requirements to only those systems legally require them, preventing compliance creep. Introduces new element (wrapper) but still treats compliance as logging practice. Might be slightly paradigm stretching? It introduces new tool but still treats compliance as logging practice. The description says isolates most restrictive requirements... preventing compliance creep into low-risk R&D prototypes. That's maybe changing relationship? Might be 2 = slightly paradigm stretching: introduces new elements but still treats compliance as logging practice. Could argue 2.\n\nOriginality (1-4): 4 not expressed before AND ingenious imaginative surprising; 3 unusual interesting shows some imagination; 2 interesting; 1 common mundane boring.\n\nDeployment wrapper for compliance is fairly common idea. Might be 2 = interesting? Or 1 common mundane? Wrapper pattern is common. I'd say 2 or 3? Probably 2 interesting. Could be 3 unusual? I think common engineering solution. Let's pick 2 = interesting. Evidence: Wrappers for regulatory logging are a familiar infrastructure pattern.\n\nEffectiveness (1-4): degree idea will solve problem. 4 reasonable and will solve stated problem without regard workability; 3 reasonable and will contribute to solution; 2 unreasonable unlikely; 1 solves unrelated.\n\nProblem: lab must decide how to meet logging mandate and/or adapt R&D accordingly. Proposal enforces logging mandates for high-risk systems per Article12(3) and isolates requirements. That directly addresses logging mandate. Should solve problem. Effectiveness 4? If you could do it, it would solve main problem. Yes. Evidence: Wrapper ensures automatic logs of period use, reference DB, input data match, verifier identity as required.\n\nApplicability (1-4): degree clearly applies to stated problem. 4 solves identified problem directly related; 3 solves implied problem related; etc. Clearly applies. So 4.\n\nProvide output with id and subscale evidence then score.\n\nNeed format: For each subscale give \"<subscale>_evidence\" first then \"<subscale>\" integer.\n\nProbably JSON? Just echo id exactly. Provide rating.\n\nLet's produce:\n\nid: P1640\nacceptability_evidence: ...\nacceptability: 4\n...\n\nEnsure one sentence evidence.\n\nMake sure sentences end with period.\n\nLet's output structured.\n\n",
