d do it, would it solve logging mandate? Semantic traceability goes beyond timestamping to capture why... Article 12 requires automatic recording of events logs over lifetime, identify situations risk, etc. Semantic traceability might exceed requirements, so would solve. So effectiveness 4 = reasonable and will solve stated problem without regard for workability.\n\nApplicability: degree clearly applies to stated problem.\n4 = solves identified problem directly related to stated problem (do X to get Y, and Y is part of stated problem)\nIt does logging. Seems directly related. Maybe 4.\n\nWe need one sentence evidence each.\n\nLet's craft outputs.\n\nAcceptability_evidence: The proposal proposes additional research logging with no legal or ethical violations and aligns with regulatory transparency goals. Score 4? Could be 4 common strategies violate no norms. Might be 4.\n\nImplementability_evidence: Logging latent activations and attention maps across high-risk model lifetimes requires substantial engineering, storage and research investment beyond standard logging. Score 2.\n\nParadigm_relatedness_evidence: It reframes compliance logging as a scientific interpretability project, changing how R&D and compliance obligations relate. Score 4? Or 3?\n\nOriginality_evidence: Evolving event logs into semantic traceability with latent space capture is unusual and imaginative for a compliance response. Score 3.\n\nEffectiveness_evidence: If realized, semantic traceability would provide the mandated logs and richer traceability, thereby meeting Article 12 requirements. Score 4.\n\nApplicability_evidence: The project directly addresses how to meet the automatic logging mandate for high-risk AI systems under Article 12. Score 4.\n\nEnsure order.\n\nReturn JSON? Probably list.\n\nLet's output as per request: echo id exactly. For each subscale give <subscale>_evidence then <subscale>.\n\nProvide lines.\n\nI'll output structured.\n\n",
