le and will solve stated problem without regard workability => 4. Could be 3 contributes? It eliminates redundant development and optimizes storage. Might be full solution. I'll give 4.\n\nImplementability: degree easily implemented. Standardized internal software library plug-and-play module... some changes or reasonably feasible measures? Developing internal library is some changes, reasonably feasible. Not easy low cost? Might be moderate. Could be 3 = some changes, or reasonably feasible measures. Not totally impossible. I think 3.\n\nAcceptability: degree socially legally politically acceptable. Common strategies violate no norms. Unified logging is common compliance strategy. Score 4.\n\nParadigm_relatedness: degree to which idea preserves/modifies paradigm anchored to this problem.\nLevels:\n4 = paradigm breaking: introduces new elements AND changes relationship between lab's R&D and its compliance obligations, or addresses larger problem of what lab researches\n3 = paradigm stretching: changes that relationship (e.g., logging woven into science, new partners or offerings born from compliance)\n2 = slightly paradigm stretching: introduces new elements (tools, formats, processes) but still treats compliance as logging practice\n1 = paradigm preserving: standard compliance and logging practice; lab's way of working is unchanged\n\nProposal introduces standardized library, common API. Still treats compliance as logging practice, introduces new tools/processes. So slightly paradigm stretching = 2.\n\nOriginality: degree rare but ingenious...\nCommon, mundane, boring? Unified logging framework is common practice. Might be interesting but common. Probably 1 = common, mundane, boring. Could be 2 = interesting. Internal software library for compliance logging is fairly standard. I'll give 1.\n\nNeed output format: echo id exactly. For each subscale give <subscale>_evidence then <subscale>. Provide integer level.\n\nProbably JSON? Instruction says return rating echoing its id. Provide for each subscale... Probably list.\n\nLet's produce:\n\nid: P2815\napplicability_evidence: ...\napplicability: 4\netc.\n\nEnsure one sentence evidence.\n\nLet's craft concise sentences.\n\nApplicability evidence: The proposal builds automated event logging to meet Article 12's lifetime logging and traceability mandate for high-risk AI systems.\n\nEffectiveness evidence: A common API that captures timestamps, input references and system events would satisfy the logging requirements without regard to implementation cost.\n\nImplementability evidence: Developing an internal plug-and-play library requires engineering effort and cross-team coordination but is a reasonably feasible internal software project.\n\nAcceptability evidence: Centralized secure logging for compliance is a standard, legally required practice that violates no norms or sensibilities.\n\nParadigm_relatedness evidence: The framework introduces new tools and processes for logging while still treating compliance as separate logging practice rather than changing R&D-compliance relationship.\n\nOriginality evidence: A standardized internal logging library for regulatory compliance is a common, mundane industry solution.\n\nScores as above.\n\nLet's output.",
