 to meet logging mandate and/or adapt R&D accordingly. Proposal is open standard for traceability metadata. Does it solve identified problem directly related? It addresses logging mandate via standards. Applicability 4 = solves an identified problem that is directly related to stated problem (do X to get Y, and Y is part of stated problem). It does help meet logging mandate. Might be implied? It's direct.\n\nEvidence: Defining interoperable formats for reference databases and verification logs directly addresses the Article 12 logging requirements.\n\nEffectiveness (1-4): degree will solve problem.\nReasonable and will solve stated problem without regard for workability? If you could do it, would it solve main problem of meeting logging mandate? Standards help but don't automatically implement logs in lab. It contributes to solution but not directly ensures own compliance. Might be 3 = reasonable and will contribute to solution (partial). Could be 4? Reasonable and will solve stated problem without regard for workability. Creating standards doesn't guarantee lab's own logs comply. So partial.\n\nEvidence: Publishing a schema improves future compliance interoperability but does not by itself implement the required automatic logging in the lab's own systems.\n\nThus scores:\nacceptability 4\nimplementability 3\noriginality 3\nparadigm_relatedness 3\napplicability 4? maybe 3? Let's think applicability anchor: 4 solves identified problem directly related. Identified problem is how to meet logging mandate and/or adapt R&D. Standards help adapt R&D, but does it solve meeting logging mandate? Indirectly. Maybe 3 solves implied problem related. Hmm.\n\nThe proposal is about establishing common language for compliance across institutions. That's directly related to meeting logging mandate? Might be applicable. I'd keep 4.\n\nEffectiveness 3.\n\nReturn rating echoing id.\n\nNeed format: For each subscale give <subscale>_evidence then <subscale>.\n\nProbably output JSON or list.\n\nProvide as:\n\nid: P1281\nacceptability_evidence: ...\nacceptability: 4\n...\n\nEnsure order listed.\n\nLet's produce final.",
